/-!
# Structurality from `Equation50` through a two-guard companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell2.py`.  `Equation50` is `x = x ◇ (x ◇ (y ◇ y))`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with `x □ y = if (M.op a a) = b then (M.op b a) else if (M.op b b) = a then (M.op b a) else (M.op a b)` is an automorphism of `◇` --
is `GuardAut2_pxx_y_pyy_x_pyx_pyx_pxy_Equation50`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation names no target, so every
law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
is 1 of them below.
